        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P38i was deassigned by"@en , "P38i foi retirada a atribuição por"@pt , "P38i ακυρώθηκε από"@el , "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property records the identifier that was deassigned from an instance of E1 CRM Entity.\nDe-assignment of an identifier may be necessary when an item is taken out of an inventory, a new numbering system is introduced or items are merged or split up. \nThe same identifier may be deassigned on more than one occasion.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The identifier assignment on 31(st) July 2001 of the silver cup OXCMS:2001.1.32 (E15) deassigned “232” (E42). (fictitious)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P38(x,y) ⇒ E15(x)\n- P38(x,y) ⇒ E42(y) \n- P38(x,y) ⇒ P141(x,y)\n"@en , "P38i a été retiré par"@fr , "P38i 被取消"@zh , "P38i wurde aufgehoben durch"@de , "P38i был отмeнeн посрeдством"@ru ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E15_Identifier_Assignment> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property records the identifier that was deassigned from an instance of E1 CRM Entity.\nDe-assignment of an identifier may be necessary when an item is taken out of an inventory, a new numbering system is introduced or items are merged or split up. \nThe same identifier may be deassigned on more than one occasion.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The identifier assignment on 31(st) July 2001 of the silver cup OXCMS:2001.1.32 (E15) deassigned “232” (E42). (fictitious)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P38(x,y) ⇒ E15(x)\n- P38(x,y) ⇒ E42(y) \n- P38(x,y) ⇒ P141(x,y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P38i был отмeнeн посрeдством"@ru , "P38i was deassigned by"@en , "P38i foi retirada a atribuição por"@pt , "P38i a été retiré par"@fr , "P38i ακυρώθηκε από"@el , "P38i 被取消"@zh , "P38i wurde aufgehoben durch"@de ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P38i_was_deassigned_by> .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#6750c56137284ae13f66b7a576153e40>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P32i ήταν τεχνική του/της"@el , "P32i was technique of"@en , "P32i был мeтодом/способом для"@ru , "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property identifies the technique or method, modelled as an instance of E55 Type, that was employed in an instance of E7 Activity. \nThese techniques should be drawn from an external E55 Type hierarchy of consistent terminology of general techniques or methods such as embroidery, oil-painting, carbon dating, etc. Specific documented techniques should be described as instances of E29 Design or Procedure.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The ornamentation of silver cup 113 (E11) used general technique gold-plating (E55). [A Design or Procedure type] (fictitious)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P32(x,y) ⇒ E7(x)\n- P32(x,y) ⇒ E55(y) \n- P32(x,y) ⇒ P125(x,y)\n"@en , "P32i war Verfahren von"@de , "P32i 是技术"@zh , "P32i foi técnica da"@pt , "P32i a été la technique générale mise en œuvre dans"@fr ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E7_Activity> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property identifies the technique or method, modelled as an instance of E55 Type, that was employed in an instance of E7 Activity. \nThese techniques should be drawn from an external E55 Type hierarchy of consistent terminology of general techniques or methods such as embroidery, oil-painting, carbon dating, etc. Specific documented techniques should be described as instances of E29 Design or Procedure.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The ornamentation of silver cup 113 (E11) used general technique gold-plating (E55). [A Design or Procedure type] (fictitious)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P32(x,y) ⇒ E7(x)\n- P32(x,y) ⇒ E55(y) \n- P32(x,y) ⇒ P125(x,y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P32i a été la technique générale mise en œuvre dans"@fr , "P32i was technique of"@en , "P32i ήταν τεχνική του/της"@el , "P32i был мeтодом/способом для"@ru , "P32i war Verfahren von"@de , "P32i 是技术"@zh , "P32i foi técnica da"@pt ;
