        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P141i a été attribué par"@fr , "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E13 Attribute Assignment with the instance of E1 CRM Entity used in the attribution. The instance of E1 CRM Entity here plays the role of the range of the attribution.\nThe kind of attribution made should be documented using P177 assigned property of type (is type of property assigned).\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The Current Ownership Assessment of Martin Doerr’s silver cup February 1997 (E13) assigned Martin Doerr (E21). (fictitious)\n- The Identifier Assignment on 1(st) June 1997 of the silver cup donated by Martin Doerr (E15) assigned 232 (E42). (fictitious)\n- The examination of MS Sinai Greek 418 (E13) assigned unsupported (E55.) (Honey & Pickwoad, 2010)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P141(x,y) ⇒ E13(x)\n- P141(x,y) ⇒ E1(y)\n"@en , "P141i foi atribuído por"@pt , "P141i wurde zugewiesen durch"@de , "P141i αποδόθηκε από"@el , "P141i was assigned by"@en , "P141i назначeн посрeдством"@ru , "P141i 被分配"@zh ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E13_Attribute_Assignment> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E13 Attribute Assignment with the instance of E1 CRM Entity used in the attribution. The instance of E1 CRM Entity here plays the role of the range of the attribution.\nThe kind of attribution made should be documented using P177 assigned property of type (is type of property assigned).\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The Current Ownership Assessment of Martin Doerr’s silver cup February 1997 (E13) assigned Martin Doerr (E21). (fictitious)\n- The Identifier Assignment on 1(st) June 1997 of the silver cup donated by Martin Doerr (E15) assigned 232 (E42). (fictitious)\n- The examination of MS Sinai Greek 418 (E13) assigned unsupported (E55.) (Honey & Pickwoad, 2010)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P141(x,y) ⇒ E13(x)\n- P141(x,y) ⇒ E1(y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P141i 被分配"@zh , "P141i was assigned by"@en , "P141i назначeн посрeдством"@ru , "P141i αποδόθηκε από"@el , "P141i foi atribuído por"@pt , "P141i a été attribué par"@fr , "P141i wurde zugewiesen durch"@de ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P141i_was_assigned_by> .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#0893cdc77ab35115d066b97a3833f55a>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P124i wurde umgewandelt durch"@de , "P124i μετατράπηκε από"@el , "P124i был трансформирован"@ru , "P124i 被转变"@zh , "P124i foi transformado por"@pt , "P124i was transformed by"@en , "Quantification of the inverse property: one to many, necessary (1,n:0,1)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property identifies the instance or instances E18 Physical Thing that have ceased to exist due to an instance of E81 Transformation.\nThe item that has ceased to exist and was replaced by the result of the Transformation. The continuity between both items, the new and the old, is expressed by the links to the common instance of E81 Transformation.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The transformation of the Venetian Loggia in Heraklion into a city hall (E81, E12) transformed the Venetian Loggia in Heraklion (E24). (Municipality of Heraklion, 2021)\n- The mummification of Tut-Ankh-Amun (E81, E12) transformed the deceased Pharaoh Tut-Ankh-Amun (E21). (Carter & Mace, 1977)\n- The death, carbonization and petrification of some people of Pompeii in 79AD by the intense heat of a pyroclastic cloud and ashes from the eruption of Mount Vesuvius (E69, E81) transformed some people of Pompeii (E21). [AND: was death of (P100) some people of Pompeii (E21).]\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ E81(x)\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ E18(y)\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ P93(x,y)\n"@en , "P124i a été transformé par"@fr ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E81_Transformation> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: one to many, necessary (1,n:0,1)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property identifies the instance or instances E18 Physical Thing that have ceased to exist due to an instance of E81 Transformation.\nThe item that has ceased to exist and was replaced by the result of the Transformation. The continuity between both items, the new and the old, is expressed by the links to the common instance of E81 Transformation.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The transformation of the Venetian Loggia in Heraklion into a city hall (E81, E12) transformed the Venetian Loggia in Heraklion (E24). (Municipality of Heraklion, 2021)\n- The mummification of Tut-Ankh-Amun (E81, E12) transformed the deceased Pharaoh Tut-Ankh-Amun (E21). (Carter & Mace, 1977)\n- The death, carbonization and petrification of some people of Pompeii in 79AD by the intense heat of a pyroclastic cloud and ashes from the eruption of Mount Vesuvius (E69, E81) transformed some people of Pompeii (E21). [AND: was death of (P100) some people of Pompeii (E21).]\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ E81(x)\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ E18(y)\n- P124(x,y) ⇒ P93(x,y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P124i was transformed by"@en , "P124i foi transformado por"@pt , "P124i a été transformé par"@fr , "P124i wurde umgewandelt durch"@de , "P124i μετατράπηκε από"@el , "P124i 被转变"@zh , "P124i был трансформирован"@ru ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P124i_was_transformed_by> .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#ad37c34a735811937bada118cc65cc69>
        a                 sh:PropertyShape ;
