        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P10i содeржит"@ru , "P10i enthält"@de , "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many, necessary, dependent (1,n:1,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E92 Spacetime Volume with another instance of E92 Spacetime Volume that falls within the latter. In other words, all points in the former are also points in the latter.\nThis property is transitive and reflexive.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The Great Plague (E4) falls within The Gothic period (E4). (Porter, 2009)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ E92(x)\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ E92(y)\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ P132(x,y)\n- P10(x,y) ∧ P10(y,z)] ⇒ P10(x,z)\n- P10(x,x)\n"@en , "P10i contém"@pt , "P10i περιλαμβάνει"@el , "P10i contains"@en , "P10i 包含"@zh , "P10i contient"@fr ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E92_Spacetime_Volume> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many, necessary, dependent (1,n:1,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E92 Spacetime Volume with another instance of E92 Spacetime Volume that falls within the latter. In other words, all points in the former are also points in the latter.\nThis property is transitive and reflexive.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The Great Plague (E4) falls within The Gothic period (E4). (Porter, 2009)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ E92(x)\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ E92(y)\n- P10(x,y) ⇒ P132(x,y)\n- P10(x,y) ∧ P10(y,z)] ⇒ P10(x,z)\n- P10(x,x)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P10i 包含"@zh , "P10i contém"@pt , "P10i contains"@en , "P10i enthält"@de , "P10i содeржит"@ru , "P10i contient"@fr , "P10i περιλαμβάνει"@el ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P10i_contains> .

