<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#dc2fa15faa347750b6eca4779625ff8d>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property specifies that the temporal extent of the domain instance A of E2 Temporal Entity ends before or simultaneously with the end of the temporal extent of the range instance B of E2 Temporal Entity. \nIn other words, if A = [A(start), A(end)] and B = [B(start), B(end)], it means A(end) ≤ B(end )is true. \nThis property is part of the set of temporal primitives P173 – P176, P182 – P185.\nThis property corresponds to a disjunction (logical OR) of the following Allen temporal relations (Allen, 1983): {before, meets, overlaps, finished by, start, equals, during, finishes}.\nThis property is irreflexive\n\n\nhttps://cidoc-crm.org/html/version_images/images_7.1.3/image_13.png\n\n\nFigure 20: Temporal entity A ends before or with the end of temporal entity B. Here A is longer than B\n\n\nhttps://cidoc-crm.org/html/version_images/images_7.1.3/image_14.png\n\n\nFigure 21: Temporal entity A ends before or with the end of temporal entity B. Here A is shorter than B\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The reign/life of Harold II (E4) ends before or with the end of the Battle of Hastings (E7)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ E2(x)\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ E2(y)\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ P174(x,y)\n- ¬P184(x,x)\n"@en , "P184i ends with or after the end of"@en , "P184i заканчиваeтся с или послe окончания"@ru , "P184i se termine au moment de ou après la fin de"@fr ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E2_Temporal_Entity> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property specifies that the temporal extent of the domain instance A of E2 Temporal Entity ends before or simultaneously with the end of the temporal extent of the range instance B of E2 Temporal Entity. \nIn other words, if A = [A(start), A(end)] and B = [B(start), B(end)], it means A(end) ≤ B(end )is true. \nThis property is part of the set of temporal primitives P173 – P176, P182 – P185.\nThis property corresponds to a disjunction (logical OR) of the following Allen temporal relations (Allen, 1983): {before, meets, overlaps, finished by, start, equals, during, finishes}.\nThis property is irreflexive\n\n\nhttps://cidoc-crm.org/html/version_images/images_7.1.3/image_13.png\n\n\nFigure 20: Temporal entity A ends before or with the end of temporal entity B. Here A is longer than B\n\n\nhttps://cidoc-crm.org/html/version_images/images_7.1.3/image_14.png\n\n\nFigure 21: Temporal entity A ends before or with the end of temporal entity B. Here A is shorter than B\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The reign/life of Harold II (E4) ends before or with the end of the Battle of Hastings (E7)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ E2(x)\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ E2(y)\n- P184(x,y) ⇒ P174(x,y)\n- ¬P184(x,x)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P184i ends with or after the end of"@en , "P184i заканчиваeтся с или послe окончания"@ru , "P184i se termine au moment de ou après la fin de"@fr ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P184i_ends_with_or_after_the_end_of> .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#5b596c13a145f49c8261dc8a11ee1dd9>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P99 löste auf"@de , "P99 διέλυσε"@el , "P99 解散了"@zh , "P99 a dissous"@fr , "P99 dissolveu"@pt , "P99 dissolved"@en , "Quantification: one to many, necessary (1,n:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property associates the instance of E68 Dissolution with the instance of E74 Group that it disbanded.\n\nExamples:\n- The end of The Hole in the Wall Gang (E68) dissolved The Hole in the Wall Gang (E74). (Patterson, 1998)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ E68(x)\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ E74(y) \n- P99(x,y) ⇒ P11(x,y)\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ P93(x,y)\n"@en , "P99 распустил"@ru ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E74_Group> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification: one to many, necessary (1,n:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property associates the instance of E68 Dissolution with the instance of E74 Group that it disbanded.\n\nExamples:\n- The end of The Hole in the Wall Gang (E68) dissolved The Hole in the Wall Gang (E74). (Patterson, 1998)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ E68(x)\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ E74(y) \n- P99(x,y) ⇒ P11(x,y)\n- P99(x,y) ⇒ P93(x,y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P99 解散了"@zh , "P99 διέλυσε"@el , "P99 распустил"@ru , "P99 dissolved"@en , "P99 löste auf"@de , "P99 a dissous"@fr , "P99 dissolveu"@pt ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P99_dissolved> .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#541fdf4ea99028fd9a89ce912273fa8a>
        a               sh:NodeShape ;
        rdfs:label      "E20 Biological Object"@en , "E20 Biologischer Gegenstand"@de , "E20 Биологичeский Объeкт"@ru , "E20 Βιολογικό Ακτικείμενο"@el , "E20 Objeto Biológico"@pt , "E20 生物对象"@zh , "E20 Objet biologique"@fr ;
        sh:description  "Scope note:\nThis class comprises individual items of a material nature, which live, have lived, or are natural products of or from living organisms. \nArtificial objects that incorporate biological elements, such as Victorian butterfly frames, can be documented as both instances of E20 Biological Object and E22 Human-Made Object.\n\nExamples:\n- me (fictitious)\n- Tut-Ankh-Amun (Edwards and Boltin, 1979)\n- Boukephalus [Horse of Alexander the Great] (Lamb, 2005)\n- petrified dinosaur excrement PA1906-344\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- E20(x) ⇒ E19(x)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "E20 Biological Object"@en , "E20 Biologischer Gegenstand"@de , "E20 生物对象"@zh , "E20 Objeto Biológico"@pt , "E20 Биологичeский Объeкт"@ru , "E20 Objet biologique"@fr , "E20 Βιολογικό Ακτικείμενο"@el ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:IRI ;
        sh:targetClass  <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E20_Biological_Object> .

