<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#26d845f1f64670cac4d1bd73e198ef0b>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P166 a été une présence de"@fr , "Quantification: many to one, necessary (1,1:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property associates an instance of E93 Presence with the instance of E92 Spacetime Volume of which it represents a temporal restriction (i.e. a time-slice). Instantiating this property constitutes a necessary part of the identity of the respective instance of E93 Presence.\n\nExamples:\n- The Roman Empire on 19(th) August AD 14 (E93) was a presence of The Roman Empire (E4). (Clare and Edwards, 1992)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ E93(x)\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ E92(y)\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ P10(x,y)\n"@en , "P166 был в присутствии"@ru , "P166 was a presence of"@en ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E92_Spacetime_Volume> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification: many to one, necessary (1,1:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property associates an instance of E93 Presence with the instance of E92 Spacetime Volume of which it represents a temporal restriction (i.e. a time-slice). Instantiating this property constitutes a necessary part of the identity of the respective instance of E93 Presence.\n\nExamples:\n- The Roman Empire on 19(th) August AD 14 (E93) was a presence of The Roman Empire (E4). (Clare and Edwards, 1992)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ E93(x)\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ E92(y)\n- P166(x,y) ⇒ P10(x,y)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P166 a été une présence de"@fr , "P166 was a presence of"@en , "P166 был в присутствии"@ru ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P166_was_a_presence_of> .

