<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#1c40c20558b7d4b89edd10f777368b56>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "P9i αποτελεί μέρος του/της"@el , "P9i faz parte de"@pt , "P9i fait partie de"@fr , "P9i bildet Teil von"@de , "P9i 组成部分"@zh , "P9i forms part of"@en , "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.\nThis property is transitive and asymmetric.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)\n- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)\n"@en , "P9i являeтся частью"@ru ;
        sh:class        <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E4_Period> ;
        sh:description  "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.\nThis property is transitive and asymmetric.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)\n- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)\n- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)\n"@en ;
        sh:name         "P9i forms part of"@en , "P9i fait partie de"@fr , "P9i faz parte de"@pt , "P9i bildet Teil von"@de , "P9i αποτελεί μέρος του/της"@el , "P9i 组成部分"@zh , "P9i являeтся частью"@ru ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P9i_forms_part_of> .

